! Two-atom silicon on the norm-conserving Si.pz-vbc.UPF with a Hubbard U of
! 6 eV on the 3p shell, atomic projectors: the real-time DFT+U case
! (notes/incompat/I100.md). Every other DFT+U input here is ultrasoft or a
! spinor, which the real-time Hubbard term does not cover; the check this
! cell is for is an identity at the superposition of atomic charges and
! Hund's-rule ns = 1/3, so it needs no pw.x reference and no SCF.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0, nosym = .true.
 /
 &electrons
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS alat
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 1 1 1 0 0 0
HUBBARD {atomic}
 U Si-3p 6.0
